    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1920 Flynn boasted two churches, a high school, a cotton gin, a hotel, and more.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/flynn-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Until 1910, classes met in a Baptist church; a two‑story school opened that year, and a new gymnasium‑auditorium complex followed in 1930.",
